Count Negative Numbers in a Sorted Matrix (LeetCode 1351)

Problem
You are given an m x n matrix grid sorted in non-increasing order both row-wise and column-wise.
Return the total number of negative numbers in the matrix.
Input: grid – 2D list of integers
Output: Integer – count of negative values

Key Idea
The task is simply to count how many elements in the matrix are negative.
Since the constraints are small (m, n ≤ 100), we can safely iterate through all elements and count those that are less than zero.
This approach is clear, readable, and efficient enough for the problem limits.

Approach
	1.	Iterate through each row in the matrix.
	2.	Iterate through each value in the row.
	3.	Count every value that is strictly less than 0.
Python’s generator expressions allow us to do this concisely in a single line.

Complexity
	•	Time: O(m · n) – every element is checked once
	•	Space: O(1) – no extra data structures are used

Edge Cases
	•	Matrix contains no negative numbers → return 0
	•	Matrix contains only negative numbers
	•	Matrix size is 1 × 1